  "notes": "List prices in USD per million tokens, read from the vendors' pages listed in sources on as_of. Modelled: standard speed, standard processing (not Batch or Flex), the short-context rate, no data-residency uplift, and Anthropic cache writes at the 5-minute rate (1.25x input). Not modelled, and each moves the estimate away from a real API bill. Lower than the bill: Anthropic's 1-hour cache write (2x input; in Claude Code transcripts read on 2026-09-30 the main sessions wrote 1-hour entries and the subagent runs 5-minute ones, but the archive does not record which one a write used, so cache-write cost can be up to 37.5% low); OpenAI prompts over 272K input tokens (2x input and cache rates and 1.5x output for the whole request, on GPT-6, GPT-5.6, GPT-5.5 and GPT-5.4); fast mode (about 2x, 2.5x on GPT-5.5; on Claude Opus 5.5, Opus 5 and Opus 4.8 only); the 10% uplift for data residency and regional endpoints (Anthropic inference_geo us, OpenAI regional processing, Bedrock and Google Cloud regional endpoints). Higher than the bill: Batch and Flex processing, which are 50% of standard. Claude models have no long-context surcharge (1M tokens at the standard price). Cache reads: Anthropic charges 0.1x input, except 0.025x on Claude Fable 5.1 and Mythos 5.1 and 0.05x on Claude Opus 5.5; OpenAI charges 0.1x, except 0.05x on GPT-6.1 Sol. Cache writes: OpenAI's GPT-6 and GPT-5.6 models charge 1.25x input; older OpenAI models have no cache-write charge (0). GPT-5.6 Sol's $4 input and $20 output (and so the gpt-5.6 alias's) are promotional, available at least through 2026-11-21. OpenAI's page calls them 20% and 33% lower than before, which is $5 and $30, so if the promotion ends the estimate runs low until this table is refreshed; the table does not expire on its own. Retired models (Claude Opus 4 and 4.1, Sonnet 4, Haiku 3.5; OpenAI codex-mini-latest, gpt-5-codex, gpt-5.1-codex, gpt-5.1-codex-max, gpt-5.1-codex-mini and gpt-5.2-codex) keep their last list price so that old sessions are priced. A model that is not listed is unpriced, never guessed: OpenAI's pro models (no cached-input price is published), o-series, GPT-4 and GPT-5.6 Cyber models, Codex's codex-auto-review, and every other vendor's models. A subscription plan is not billed per token: the estimate is what the same tokens would cost at API list price.",
